# Independent Plan Browser toolbar controls

Separate the graph and contextual-help controls so interaction feedback and actions cannot leak between them.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Graph and help are implemented as separate controls rather than a shared interactive container.
- [x] Tapping or pressing Graph does not animate, bounce, highlight, or invoke Help.
- [x] Tapping or pressing Help does not animate, bounce, highlight, or invoke Graph.
- [x] Each control retains an adequate, non-overlapping tap target and accessible label.
- [x] Graph navigation behavior remains consistent with the currently implemented SCR-003 scope.
- [x] Automated interaction coverage compiles for both directions.
- [ ] Focused UI checks pass on a functioning simulator.

## Scope notes

- This supersedes the earlier hit-target-only interpretation in TASK-011; pressed-state independence is required as well.

## Evidence

- Replaced the shared `ToolbarItemGroup` with two independent trailing `ToolbarItem` buttons and independent plain pressed states.
- Retained distinct accessibility identifiers/labels and the current unavailable-graph no-op behavior.
- Existing UI coverage taps Graph and verifies no Help alert, then independently opens and dismisses Help.
- The app, unit-test, and UI-test bundles compile via `xcodebuild build-for-testing -quiet` using `/private/tmp/Catanalyst-tasks018-024-derived`.
